<BaseLayout title="How we research emergency equipment" description="Our documentary research method: manufacturer specifications, Canadian offer identity, unresolved limits, concept illustrations and affiliate-link decisions.">
  <article class="container section stack methodology">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'How we research' }]} />
    <h1>How we research equipment</h1>
    <p class="label">Updated <time datetime="2026-11-01">November 1, 2026</time></p>
    <p>ApocalypseGearLab is a documentary preparedness research project. We organize equipment around power outages, household disruptions and evacuation tasks. A useful profile explains what the equipment can do, which conditions matter and what remains unresolved. Our sector names and concept art provide a visual theme; they are not evidence of protection from fictional or real disasters.</p>
    <section><h2>Selection starts with a task</h2><p>We select existing equipment to investigate a practical need, such as lighting a room, storing drinking water or carrying supplies. We compare documented capacity, portability, required accessories and operating limits. Inclusion in the catalogue is not a ranking, endorsement or statement that everyone needs the item. We do not invent prices, discounts, review scores or stock levels.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Specifications and manufacturer documentation</h2><p>Research records identify manufacturer pages and manuals, the model or revision, specification units, operating conditions and safety limits. We distinguish stored energy from output power, nominal figures from measured performance, and component compatibility from suitability for a hazard. Manufacturer documentation describes a model; it does not authenticate a delivered unit. Source dates record an actual research visit and are not refreshed on every build.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Canadian offers and buying links</h2><p>Amazon.ca references are recorded by ASIN. Where evidence exists, we compare the model, revision, package quantity, accessories and regional electrical details. Owner-supplied documents are labelled separately from an independent inspection of a current offer. Sellers and selected variants can change. An available affiliate link means the recorded link is permitted under our current link policy, not that the current offer, seller or supplied product has been independently verified.</p><p>Unresolved mandatory safety or model holds keep buying links unavailable. A profile’s editorial approval, retailer evidence, safety status and link availability are separate decisions. Search-engine indexability is also reviewed separately; a buying link cannot grant editorial publication or indexing approval.</p></section>
    <section><h2>What we have not established</h2><p>Unless a profile explicitly documents otherwise, products have not been physically tested by us. Manufacturer claims are not our laboratory results. We do not claim ownership, professional credentials, certification, manufacturer endorsement or user testimonials. Unknown performance, incomplete manuals, package conflicts and unverified certifications remain stated on the relevant profile. Safety-critical choices need the exact instructions and, where appropriate, qualified professional advice.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Why we use concept illustrations</h2><p>Illustrations help distinguish equipment and maintain the site’s visual identity. They are labelled as concept artwork and can contain decorative or inaccurate details. An illustration does not prove model identity, markings, accessories, certification or package contents. Read the caption and documentary specifications, then compare the actual offer and delivered label.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Affiliate commissions</h2><p>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases. Eligible buttons lead to Amazon.ca and are labelled as affiliate links. A commission does not establish product suitability or remove a documented hold. Read the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure and account declaration</a> for the current commercial context.</p></section>
    <section id="corrections"><h2>Corrections and maintenance</h2><p>To report an error, <a href="https://github.com/ApocalypseGearLab/apocalypsegearlab.github.io/issues/new">open a repository issue</a> with the profile URL, model or ASIN, the specific statement and a manufacturer or official reference. GitHub requires an account; avoid including personal order details. We review the cited evidence before changing a specification, safety decision or link. A visible updated date means that page’s content was maintained on that date; it is not a fresh check of every product or offer.</p></section>
    <p><a href="/gear/">Explore equipment profiles</a> or choose <a href="/blackout/">BLACKOUT power planning</a>, <a href="/fallout/">FALLOUT household supplies</a> or <a href="/outbreak/">OUTBREAK evacuation planning</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
